{"toolCallId":"call_2d80b954fe7147d48696d62117004028","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"64:| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"2f57be","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2daa8fa746f64d0b8e99fdaaa117efa3","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"57-| `CONTINUITY_FRESHNESS` | WARNING | completion claims | Opt-in strict-only completion freshness check |\n58-| `ANCHORS_VALID`      | ERROR    | spec docs with anchored templates | Anchors present, paired and not nested (adr-NNN may hold adr-NNN-*) |\n59-| `FOLDER_NAMING`      | ERROR    | Folder path   | Folder follows ###-short-name convention       |\n60-| `FRONTMATTER_VALID`  | ERROR    | spec docs     | YAML frontmatter properly structured           |\n61-| `COMPLEXITY_MATCH`   | WARNING  | All levels    | Content metrics match declared level           |\n62:| `AI_PROTOCOLS`       | ERROR    | Level 3/3+    | AI execution protocols present                 |\n63-| `LEVEL_MATCH`        | ERROR    | All files     | Level consistent across all spec files         |\n64-| `SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY` | ERROR  | spec docs, goal.md | Anchor sufficiency; for `goal.md` also the durable budget (one limit: fail past 4000) and binding-row existence |\n65-| `FRONTMATTER_VALUES` | WARNING  | packet docs   | `contextType` or `importance_tier` outside sk-create-frontmatter's `frontmatter-values.json`; aliases are legal |\n66-| `SOURCE_TAGS`        | WARNING  | research/ + review/ | `[SOURCE: path:line]` tags that name a gone file, a moved file or a line past the end, in packets created after the cutoff |\n67-\n68-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n69-\n70-### AC_CLOSURE\n71-\n72-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n73-\n74-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n75-\n76-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n77-\n78-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n79-\n80-**Failure modes:**\n81-\n82-| Condition | Result |\n83-|---|---|\n84-| Post-cutoff packet with no `acceptance-criteria.md` | `fail` — the document is required at these levels |\n85-| A row marked `Waived` or `Superseded` naming no ADR | `fail` — an unbacked waiver is not a pass |\n86-| A criterion row that cannot be parsed, or an unbalanced code fence | `fail` — a dropped row would empty the table and close the packet |\n87-| Duplicate criterion ids | `fail` — the tally is ambiguous |\n88-| A row citing an ADR that `decision-record.md` does not contain | `fail` — the record is the whole justification |\n89-| A packet claiming completion with an `Unmet` row | `fail` — this is the closure gate |\n90-| An `Unmet` row while the packet is still in progress | `info` — work in progress is expected to carry open criteria |\n91-| Pre-cutoff packet | `info` — grandfathered |\n92-\n--\n627-2. **Reduce scope:** Split complex specs into multiple smaller specs\n628-3. **Add content:** For sparse specs, add missing user stories, phases, or tasks\n629-\n630----\n631-\n632:## 10. AI_PROTOCOLS\n633-\n634-**Severity:** ERROR\n635-**Description:** Validates that Level 3 and 3+ specs include AI execution protocol sections for agent guidance. For Level 3+, missing protocol components are reported as errors.\n636-\n637-### Required for Level 3+\n638-\n639-| Component             | Location        | Purpose                           |\n640-| --------------------- | --------------- | --------------------------------- |\n641-| AI Execution section  | plan/tasks.md   | Main protocol header              |\n642-| Pre-Task Checklist    | plan/tasks.md   | Steps before starting any task    |\n643-| Execution Rules       | plan/tasks.md   | TASK-SEQ, TASK-SCOPE constraints  |\n644-| Status Format         | plan/tasks.md   | How to report progress            |\n645-| Blocked Protocol      | plan/tasks.md   | What to do when stuck             |\n646-\n647-### Scoring\n648-\n649-- Level 3: Should have protocol section (warning if missing)\n650-- Level 3+: Must have at least 3/4 components (error if fewer)\n651-- Phase parent: skipped. Under the lean trio policy its `plan.md` and `tasks.md` live in the child folders, which carry the protocol.\n652-\n653-### Detection Patterns\n654-\n655-```markdown\n656-## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL         ← Main section\n657-### Pre-Task Checklist           ← Component 1\n658-### Execution Rules              ← Component 2\n659-### Status Reporting Format      ← Component 3\n660-### Blocked Task Protocol        ← Component 4\n661-```\n662-\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"e79fc4","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2dbbf68c3c20423d84dabb51a7418507","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"===\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-closure.sh:9:# Rule: AC_CLOSURE\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-closure.sh:32:    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE:-true}\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-closure.sh:37:            _ACC_FLAG_NOTE=\"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE='$raw' is not a boolean; the gate stayed enabled\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-closure.sh:49:    local raw=\"${SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF:-$_ACC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT}\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ac-closure.sh:55:    _ACC_CUTOFF_NOTE=\"SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF='$raw' is not an ISO date; using $_ACC_CUTOFF_DEFAULT\"\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"04211b","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2e977c5fab9c41d396260ec377e06af0","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"        what: `spec folder -> ${basename}`,\n        apply: () => {\n          const current = readForWrite(summary);\n          const hit = SPEC_FOLDER_ROW.exec(current);\n          if (!hit) throw new Error('the Spec Folder row moved between the report and the write');\n          writeAtomic(summary, current.slice(0, hit.index) + hit[1] + basename + hit[3] + current.slice(hit.index + hit[0].length));\n        },\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  const description = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n  const descriptionText = readIfPresent(description);\n  if (descriptionText !== null) {\n    let data = null;\n    try {\n      data = JSON.parse(descriptionText);\n    } catch {\n      // Unparseable metadata is a shape failure the validator reports, and\n      // rewriting one field of a file that cannot be read would guess at the rest.\n    }\n    if (data && typeof data === 'object' && !Array.isArray(data) && typeof data.specFolder === 'string' && data.specFolder !== pointer) {\n      actions.push({\n        file: description,\n        what: `description specFolder -> ${pointer}`,\n        apply: () => {\n          const current = JSON.parse(readForWrite(description));\n          current.specFolder = pointer;\n          writeAtomic(description, `${JSON.stringify(current, null, 2)}\\n`);\n        },\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  // A packet sitting directly in an archive has no parent packet: z_archive is\n  // not one, and a re-derive computes null. The graph merge keeps a stored\n  // parent over a null re-derive and flags it for review, so after a move the\n  // parent the packet was archived from would survive and fail the path check.\n  const graph = path.join(folder, 'graph-metadata.json');\n  const graphText = path.basename(path.dirname(path.resolve(REPO, folder))) === 'z_archive' ? readIfPresent(graph) : null;\n  if (graphText !== null) {\n    let data = null;\n    try {\n      data = JSON.parse(graphText);\n    } catch {\n      // A graph file that cannot be read is the re-derive's to report.\n    }\n    if (data && typeof data === 'object' && !Array.isArray(data) && data.parent_id) {\n      actions.push({\n        file: graph,\n        what: `graph parent ${data.parent_id} -> none, the packet is archived`,\n        apply: () => {\n          const current = JSON.parse(readForWrite(graph));\n          current.parent_id = null;\n          delete current.parent_id_review_required;\n          writeAtomic(graph, `${JSON.stringify(current, null, 2)}\\n`);\n        },\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const name of DOCS) {\n    const file = path.join(folder, name);\n    const text = readIfPresent(file);\n    if (text === null) continue;\n    const hit = POINTER_LINE.exec(text);\n    if (!hit || hit.index >= frontmatterEnd(text) || hit[3] === pointer) continue;\n    actions.push({\n      file,\n      what: `packet pointer -> ${pointer}`,\n      apply: () => {\n        const current = readForWrite(file);\n        const found = POINTER_LINE.exec(current);\n        if (!found || found.index >= frontmatterEnd(current)) {\n          throw new Error('the packet pointer left the frontmatter between the report and the write');\n        }\n        writeAtomic(file, `${current.slice(0, found.index)}${found[1]}\"${pointer}\"${current.slice(found.index + found[0].length)}`);\n      },\n    });\n  }\n  return actions;\n}\n\nasync function rederive(folder) {\n  try {\n    await run('node', ['--import', TSX_LOADER, BACKFILL, folder], CHILD);\n    return null;\n  } catch (err) {\n    return childFailure(err);\n  }\n}\n\n// A JSON parse error's message quotes the bytes around the fault, so a failed write\n// is reported by the kind of failure alone. Other messages come from this file or\n// from the file system, and file system errors carry a code.\nfunction failureKind(err) {\n  if (err instanceof SyntaxError) return 'not valid JSON';\n  return err.code || err.message;\n}\n\nasync function repairFolder(folder, apply) {\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"57b4e9","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2f0dc92eeb0d4462bb6e852d5a750eab","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"anchor-generator.ts\nascii-boxes.ts\ncompletion-state.cjs\ncontent-filter.ts\ndecision-tree-generator.ts\ndist-freshness.cjs\nesm-entry.mjs\nesm-entry.ts\nflowchart-generator.ts\nfrontmatter-grandfather-allowlist.json\nfrontmatter-migration.ts\ngit-branch.sh\nmemory-frontmatter.ts\nmemory-telemetry.ts\nparse-bool-flag.sh\nphase-classifier.ts\nREADME.md\nsemantic-signal-extractor.ts\nsemantic-summarizer.ts\nsession-activity-signal.ts\nshell-common.sh\nsimulation-factory.ts\nstatus-classifier.sh\ntemplate-utils.sh\ntopic-keywords.ts\ntrack-roots.mjs\ntrigger-extractor.ts\ntrigger-phrase-sanitizer.ts\ntruncate-on-word-boundary.ts\nunicode-normalization.ts\n---\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"f3ea66","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2f8fc79c881247a1a4cc1e8676daffe1","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-ai-protocols.sh\n===\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-AI-PROTOCOLS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Rule: AI_PROTOCOLS\n# Severity: warn\n# Description: Validates that AI execution protocols are present for\n#   Level 3+ specs that require them.\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. HELPER FUNCTIONS\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Extract level from spec.md\n# Support multiple level declaration formats:\n# Bullet (- **Level**: N), table row (| **Level** | N |), frontmatter (level: N)\n_ai_get_declared_level() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local spec_file=\"$folder/spec.md\"\n    if [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]]; then\n        local level_line\n        # Try bullet format first: - **Level**: N\n        level_line=$(grep -E \"^\\- \\*\\*Level\\*\\*:\" \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n        # Try table format: | **Level** | N |\n        if [[ -z \"$level_line\" ]]; then\n            level_line=$(grep -Ei '^\\| *\\*\\*Level\\*\\* *\\|' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n        fi\n        # Try frontmatter YAML: level: N\n        if [[ -z \"$level_line\" ]]; then\n            level_line=$(grep -Ei '^level:' \"$spec_file\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n        fi\n        if [[ -n \"$level_line\" ]]; then\n            local level_val=\"\"\n            # Extract value based on detected format\n            if echo \"$level_line\" | grep -qE '^\\- \\*\\*Level\\*\\*:'; then\n                # Bullet: - **Level**: 3\n                level_val=$(echo \"$level_line\" | head -1 | sed 's/.*\\*\\*Level\\*\\*: *//' | tr -d '[:space:]' | sed 's/\\[.*\\]//' | head -c 2)\n            elif echo \"$level_line\" | grep -qEi '^\\|.*[Ll]evel'; then\n                # Table: | **Level** | 3 | — extract second column\n                level_val=$(echo \"$level_line\" | head -1 | awk -F'|' '{gsub(/[[:space:]*]/, \"\", $3); print $3}' | head -c 2)\n            elif echo \"$level_line\" | grep -qEi '^level:'; then\n                # Frontmatter YAML: level: 3\n                level_val=$(echo \"$level_line\" | head -1 | sed 's/^[Ll]evel: *//' | tr -d '[:space:]' | head -c 2)\n            fi\n            echo \"$level_val\"\n        fi\n    fi\n}\n\n# Check for AI protocol sections in various forms\n_ai_has_protocol_section() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n\n    # Check plan.md\n    if [[ -f \"$folder/plan.md\" ]]; then\n        if grep -qE \"AI EXECUTION|Pre-Task Checklist|Task Execution Rules\" \"$folder/plan.md\" 2>/dev/null; then\n            return 0\n        fi\n    fi\n\n    # Check tasks.md\n    if [[ -f \"$folder/tasks.md\" ]]; then\n        if grep -qE \"AI EXECUTION|Pre-Task Checklist|Blocked Task Protocol\" \"$folder/tasks.md\" 2>/dev/null; then\n            return 0\n        fi\n    fi\n\n    return 1\n}\n\n# Check for pre-task checklist\n_ai_has_pre_task_checklist() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    if [[ -f \"$folder/plan.md\" ]]; then\n        grep -q \"Pre-Task Checklist\" \"$folder/plan.md\" 2>/dev/null && return 0\n    fi\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"bc4233","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
