{"toolCallId":"call_54d270c22d5f4d6fb15cf63b956fc62c","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"// Rules this tool can settle from repository state alone. Anything absent from\n// this list is reported and left alone, however mechanical it may look.\n//\n// The validator registry already classifies every rule, and this list is not\n// simply its structural category. Two deliberate differences, recorded here so\n// the next reader does not have to guess whether they were intended:\n//\n//   GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE is structural and included, because the re-derive\n//   rewrites the very file it makes assertions about.\n//\n//   SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY is classified as an authored-template rule and included\n//   anyway, because one of its two failure modes is a recorded location that\n//   has gone stale — recomputable — while the other is a reference to a file\n//   that no longer exists, which is not. Only the first is repaired; a packet\n//   failing solely on the second is reported as beyond this tool rather than\n//   passing silently.\nconst DERIVABLE = new Set([\n  'DESCRIPTION_SHAPE',\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY',\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT',\n  'GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE',\n  'METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY',\n  'SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY',\n]);\n\n// The subset a re-derive can actually settle, because they are assertions about\n// graph-metadata.json itself. The others describe description.json contents and\n// in-document reference paths, which a re-derive does not write; planning one\n// for them would be a write that changes nothing and a report line that never\n// clears.\nconst REDERIVABLE = new Set([\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY',\n  'GENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT',\n  'GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE',\n  'METADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY',\n]);\n\nconst POINTER_LINE = /^([ \\t]*packet_pointer:[ \\t]*)([\"']?)([^\"'\\r\\n]*)([\"']?)[ \\t]*\\r?$/m;\nconst SPEC_FOLDER_ROW = /(\\|[ \\t]*\\*\\*Spec Folder\\*\\*[ \\t]*\\|[ \\t]*)([^|\\r\\n]+?)([ \\t]*\\|)/;\nconst DOCS = ['spec.md', 'plan.md', 'tasks.md', 'implementation-summary.md', 'handover.md'];\nconst PACKET_MARKERS = new Set(['spec.md', 'implementation-summary.md']);\n\n// A marker alone is not enough: the metadata writer this script drives also\n// requires the numbered folder name, and handing it a folder it will refuse\n// turns a correctly out-of-scope directory into a reported failure. The two\n// definitions of \"packet\" have to agree or the failure count means nothing.\n// Mirrors SPEC_FOLDER_RE in backfill-graph-metadata.ts.\nconst PACKET_NAME_RE = /^\\d{3}(?:[-_].+)?$/;\n\n// The recorded location lives in the leading YAML block. A pointer written into\n// a document's body is an illustration of the format, not this packet's own\n// record, and rewriting it would corrupt the passage it explains. The block can\n// sit behind a template-source HTML comment, so the opener is matched past\n// leading comments and blank lines rather than demanded at byte zero. Every\n// repeat here consumes a newline, so the group cannot loop on an empty match.\nconst FRONTMATTER_OPEN = /^\\uFEFF?(?:[ \\t]*\\r?\\n|<!--[\\s\\S]*?-->[ \\t]*\\r?\\n)*---[ \\t]*\\r?\\n/;\nconst FRONTMATTER_CLOSE = /^(?:---|\\.\\.\\.)[ \\t]*\\r?$/m;\n\nconst USAGE = 'Usage: repair-derived.cjs [--folder <packet>]... [--roots <dir>] [--apply]';\n\n// Reported as one planned step like any other, so a dry run names it and the\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1f650e","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_60614f4578984a069e9318f6b3c6c1cc","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"FAIL — 52 placeholder pattern(s) found in specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:19: [SESSION-ID]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:39: [PACKET-ID]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:41: [Draft/In Progress/Complete]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:79: [Yes/No]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md:59: [Created/Modified/Deleted]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md:77: [What was decided]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md:87: [Validation, lint, tests, manual check]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md:95: [Limitation]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:57: [Component 1]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:58: [Component 2]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:61: [Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:99: [Components/functions]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:100: [API endpoints/flows]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:101: [User journeys]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:111: [System/Library]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:119: [Conditions requiring rollback]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:120: [How to revert changes]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:152: [Low/Med/High]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:153: [Low/Med/High]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:154: [Low/Med/High]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:169: [Immediate action - e.g., disable feature flag]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:170: [Revert code - e.g., git revert or redeploy previous version]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:171: [Verify rollback - e.g., smoke test critical paths]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:172: [Notify stakeholders - if user-facing]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:175: [Yes/No]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:203: [Component A]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:204: [Component B]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:205: [Component C]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:206: [Component D]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:214: [Phase/Task]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:215: [Phase/Task]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:216: [Phase/Task]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:218: [Sum of durations]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:221: [Task A]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:222: [Task C]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:232: [Setup Complete]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:233: [Core Done]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:234: [Release Ready]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:241: [Decision Title]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:243: [Proposed/Accepted/Deprecated]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:245: [What problem we're solving]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:247: [What we decided]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:250: [Positive outcome 1]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:251: [Negative outcome + mitigation]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/plan.md:254: [Option B]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:44: [Implement core feature 1]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:45: [Implement core feature 2]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:46: [Implement core feature 3]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:47: [Add error handling]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:245: [Name]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:246: [Name]\n  specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:247: [Name]\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"0f98c2","exit_code":1,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
