{"toolCallId":"call_c35f27fe3f1b4ebbaad3f638c7f7fc26","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"307:## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n308-\n309-### Pre-Task Checklist\n310-- [ ] Read `tasks.md` and confirm the task id, its file, its quoted anchor and its line number.\n311-- [ ] Re-read the file the task edits; confirm the quoted anchor is still on the named line and belongs to the job the task names.\n312-- [ ] Confirm the task is not `[B]`; if it is, record the blocker and stop before editing.\n313-- [ ] Confirm the value comes from `scratch/r24/timeouts.md`, never from a sibling job and never from this plan.\n314-\n315-### Execution Rules\n316-| Rule | Description |\n317-|------|-------------|\n318-| TASK-SEQ | Run T001 to T102 in order. The only `[B]` task is T003, and its blocker is another phase. |\n319-| TASK-SCOPE | Write only `.github/workflows/*.yml`, `.github/workflows/README.md` and this phase's `scratch/`. Every other path is read-only. |\n320-| TASK-PROOF | Run the task's check and read both its output and its exit status before marking the task `[x]`. |\n321-| TASK-ANCHOR | Locate the quoted text. A moved line is not a changed edit; an absent anchor is a stop, not a nearby edit. |\n322-| TASK-COMMENT | No workflow comment, step name, job name or README sentence added by this phase carries an R-id, a D-id or a phase number. |\n323-\n324-### Status Reporting Format\n325-After each task: `Task T### complete. Files: <paths>. Proof: <command> -> <observed output/exit>.` At a phase boundary, report the task range, the files changed and the gate that passed.\n326-\n327-### Blocked Task Protocol\n328-If a task cannot run, stop and record the blocker in `scratch/phase-result.md` with the task id, the command that failed and its output. Do not substitute a different file, a different value or a different command. A `[B]` task stays blocked until its dependency's proof exists; a failed gate is repaired, not waived.\n329-\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"3b4cab","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_c66b66f6664a43dda353f33b22884035","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts:1059:function extractDescriptionWithFolderFallback(specContent: string, folderPath: string): string {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1060-  const folderName = path.basename(folderPath);\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1061-  return extractDescription(specContent)\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1062-    || slugifyFolderName(folderName).replace(/-/g, ' ')\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1063-    || folderName;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1064-}\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1065-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1066-// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1067-// 7b. PER-FOLDER DESCRIPTION OPERATIONS\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1068-// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1069-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1070-/**\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1071- * Generate a PerFolderDescription by reading the spec.md in a folder.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1072- * Preserves memorySequence and memoryNameHistory from existing description.json.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1073- *\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1074- * @param folderPath - Absolute path to the spec folder.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1075- * @param basePath   - Absolute path to the specs root directory.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1076- * @returns A PerFolderDescription, or null if spec.md is unreadable.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1077- */\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1078-export function generatePerFolderDescription(\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1079-  folderPath: string,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1080-  basePath: string,\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1081-): PerFolderDescription | null {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1082-  // Path containment check, prevent directory traversal attacks\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1083-  const realFolder = resolveRealPathSafe(path.resolve(folderPath));\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1084-  const realBase = resolveRealPathSafe(path.resolve(basePath));\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1085-  // Equality check covers the case where folderPath IS basePath; path.sep boundary\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1086-  // Prevents prefix bypass (e.g. /specs-evil passing for /specs).\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1087-  if (!realFolder || !realBase || !(realFolder === realBase || realFolder.startsWith(realBase + path.sep))) {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1088-    return null;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1089-  }\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1090-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1091-  const specMdPath = path.join(folderPath, 'spec.md');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1092-  let content: string;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1093-  try {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1094-    content = fs.readFileSync(specMdPath, 'utf-8');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1095-  } catch (_error: unknown) {\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1096-    return null;\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1097-  }\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1098-\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/search/folder-discovery.ts-1099-  const folderName = path.basename(folderPath);\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"122740","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
